$[ set.mm $]

$( ac9s: An Axiom of Choice equivalent.

   Calculational proof (structured derivation) of:
     |-( A. x e. A B =/= (/) <-> X_ x e. A B =/= (/) )
   under hypothesis  A e. _V.

   Format: each step line is an opaque Metamath token sequence with an
   optional justification { by <rule> using <rules> }.  The mmcalc parser
   does not interpret any tokens (relations like <->, the turnstile |-,
   parentheses, ... are just data); expression structure is recovered only
   via TOPLEVEL parsing using the rules in the .settings file.

   This is based on the metamathematics of ~ ac9s in set.mm.
   The proof tokens are the UNCOMPRESSED label sequence, as produced by
     metamath 'show proof ac9s /normal'
   with the hypothesis label ac9.1 renamed to myac9.1 to avoid a clash
   with the existing ac9.1 in set.mm.  Each step applies a statement
   which pops its own mandatory hypotheses off the proof stack. $)

$( Context / theorem declaration (machine-verifiable part) $)

${
  $d f x A $.  $d f B $.
  myac9.1 $e |- A e. _V $.
  myac9s $p |- ( A. x e. A B =/= (/) <-> X_ x e. A B =/= (/) ) $=
    cB c0 wne vx cA wral vx cA cB cixp c0 wne
    cB c0 wne vx cA wral vf cv cA wfn vx cv vf cv
    cfv cB wcel vx cA wral wa vf wex vx cA cB cixp
    c0 wne vx cA cB vf myac9.1 ac6s4 vx cA cB cixp
    c0 wne vf cv vx cA cB cixp wcel vf wex vf cv
    cA wfn vx cv vf cv cfv cB wcel vx cA wral wa
    vf wex vf vx cA cB cixp n0 vf cv vx cA cB cixp
    wcel vf cv cA wfn vx cv vf cv cfv cB wcel vx
    cA wral wa vf vx cA cB vf cv vf vex elixp exbii
    bitr2i sylib vx cA cB ixpn0 impbii $.
$}

$( Calculational proof:

   Starting from  X_ x e. A B =/= (/)  we show it is equivalent to
   A. x e. A B =/= (/).  The key ping-pong argument introduces a fresh
   variable f and the double implication at the end (impbii). $)

X_ x e. A B =/= (/)
    <-> { by (n0) using (bicomi) } (bitri)
    E. f f e. X_ x e. A B
    <-> { by (elixp) and (vex) using (bitcomi) and (exbii) } (sylib)
    E. f ( f Fn A /\ A. x e. A ( f ` x ) e. B )
    <- { by (ac6s4) and (myac9.1) } (impbii)
    A. x e. A B =/= (/)
    <- { by (ixpn0) } 
    X_ x e. A B =/= (/)
    .